ata types as chris mentioned  with big data cloud-based data analysis  tools  coding exercises and r and python as  well as  project-based tutorials that combine  biological or biomedical topics with  data analytics  statistical analysis principles and  curated data sets  in a variety of applications and so what  our company really does is provides an  opportunity for recent graduates  and students to leverage their skills in  bioinformatics and computational biology  to train and mentor others with a  growing community of over 7 000 students  worldwide  and now a growing community in louisiana  which we're very excited about  and so the academic oversight for work  is ensured by a close collaboration with  the tower bioinformatics research center  which is at university of haifa  in israel and is directed by dr alfred  album dr lina brodsky  so the center recently signed a  memorandum of understanding with  louisiana state university  to collaborate on research projects  expand these training programs and  establish  faculty and student exchange programs so  hopefully  this will be possible after the pandemic  but also due to the increased online  opportunities that have been highlighted  due to these unfortunate events as we  can see here in this virtual conference  hopefully virtual use of these resources  will be enhanced  so let me introduce the specific  solutions that we have been focused on  for the past several years  recently as was mentioned by chris lbrm  has started offering research licenses  to the tbi info platform  which provides a simple and intuitive  user interface  for processing analysis and machine  learning methods for integration of  multi-onyx data  and to support the growing number of  users we're now offering processing the  data on our shared server infrastructure  as well as on google cloud so now we can  run pipelines on our servers  or you can send them to google cloud  directly and so we're now developing  pipelines that support the 