ourse  collections  that also break down the analytical and  different machine learning methods  into very short tutorials for  asynchronous use  and so we hope to increase using these  resources the capacity  for data mining and machine learning  methods so that those could be used  effectively to analyze  big data sets and do predictive analysis  and together with lbrn we're going to  start offering  these courses as program resources  they will be offered eventually with  lbrn certification  and we're now working with a number of  faculty  throughout the lbrn campuses to help  integrate these asynchronous courses  into curricula offered throughout the  different puis  so to kind of briefly share with you  how we have used these materials over  the past year  and what are some of the ways that the  lbrm community can gain  access to these resources and materials  so as a part of our collaboration with  lbrn  we have this online complete  asynchronous course  that can be accessed by students  throughout the year at any time  starting with an introduction to  bioinformatics and learning about the  logic of data analysis  in application to various omics data  types so this is available  and i think we recently made an  announcement about that  so we will soon announce how people can  actually start that process  these basic materials are offered as an  introduction to bioinformatics module  which can be accessible to life science  students without  any previous experience in  bioinformatics the module covers the  basics of genomics in biomedical  applications  and we recently started the process of  offering this course as an undergraduate  course through the department of  biological sciences at lsu  and it can also be made available for  other campuses that might want to use it  as a gentle introduction to  bioinformatics  the coursework itself was developed  internally primarily but also  other contributors included faculty  such as this course on biomedical data 